 "forward": {
  "title": "Starting today",
  "lead": "The school district’s debt tax is 22.65 mills. It brings in about $6.34 million a year. Payments in 2027 are about $3.8 million.",
  "points": [
   "Under the current plan the debt tax never retires: the high-school payment doubles, to about $3.8 million a year, in 2048 — the same year the older bonds are paid off.",
   "The high-school bonds: $37.17 million borrowed, $74.54 million paid back by 2056. The interest (about $37.4 million) is more than the building.",
   "Once debt-free, the same 22.65 mills could pay cash for a $37 million school about every 5½ years.",
   "Clark County’s road bonds were sold in 2021 at 1.125–2.00%. At rates that low, borrowing costs little — saving first would have saved about $2 million."
  ],
